OK, it appears I fixed the problem in the 1st sampler I commented about.  Nimble now specifies posterior predictive branch samplers for psi, p, sigma, and s, and assigns no sampler to z. If I manually set the samplers for psi, p, sigma, and s back to random walk updates and add a binary update for z, nimble no longer tries to update y.true on it's own and everything works as I intended.

Ben

===== Monitors =====
thin = 1: G.mu, G.sigma, n, N, p, psi, sigma, sigma.obs
thin2 = 1: ID, u
===== Samplers =====
RW sampler (678)
  - tau.obs[]  (3 elements)
  - G.true[]  (675 elements)

posterior_predictive_branch sampler (453)

  - psi
  - p
  - sigma
  - s[]  (450 elements)
conjugate sampler (6)
  - G.mu[]  (3 elements)
  - G.tau[]  (3 elements)

