Hi all,

Hope everything is going well with you.

I would like to fit a DP mixture of products of normals. The model is attached below, which is not complicated. I checked the General Multivariate Models <https://r-nimble.org/bayesian-nonparametric-models-in-nimble-general-multivariate-models> example posted on Nimble's web. My confusion is that, in that example, each individual has his or her own model parameters:

for(i in 1:n) {
   for(j in 1:J) {
        y[i, j] ~ dpois( lambda[xi[i],  j] )
   }
}
for(i in 1:n) {
   for(j in 1:J) {
        lambda[i, j] ~ dgamma( shape = 1, rate = 0.1 )
   }
 }

How can I model individuals in the same cluster using the cluster-specific parameters?

Best,
Meng

